  id: ssd_m2
  displayName: Storage Drive (M.2 SSD)
  category: 3
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  mlLabel: ssd
  mlAliases: []
  specChips:
  - M.2 2280
  - NVMe
  - 1 TB
  shortDescription: "Stores the operating system, apps and files \u2014 even when
    the power is off."
  whatItDoes: An NVMe SSD stores data in flash memory chips and talks to the CPU
    over PCIe, which makes it many times faster than a hard drive.
  keyFacts:
  - "Plugs straight into the motherboard \u2014 no cables"
  - Uses the M-key M.2 slot
  - Held down by a small screw or latch
  installationSteps:
  - Remove the M.2 heatsink or screw if present.
  - "Insert the SSD at about 30\xB0 into the slot."
  - Press it flat.
  - Secure with the screw or latch.
  safetyTip: Don't overtighten the tiny M.2 screw.
  model3DPrefab: {fileID: 6320624813473873214, guid: 41e5fdf4dea24044dbbd32857a80921b, type: 3}
